Subject: winex11, server: add touchpad pinch and fixed-point wheel delivery

Turn an XInput2 2.4 pinch into Ctrl+wheel without creating Ctrl key events.
Maintain the Ctrl state that applications can read, release it on every known
end path, and send no pinch wheel output while a mouse button is held. Limit
each update and cancellation correction to one notch.

Add wheel delivery at a supplied screen point without moving the cursor. A
fixed-point message keeps its source window and point, ignores later capture,
does not create raw input, does not merge, and is dropped when a mouse button
is held or the source window is no longer usable.

Limit ordinary queued wheel merging to one notch and keep vertical and
horizontal messages under the same rule.

See notes/ABLETON-WINE-POINTER-GESTURES.md for the complete safety contract.
---
